DLL: Pop
Further extend the DoublyLinkedList class by adding a pop method that removes the last node from the list and returns it.

The method should perform the following tasks:

If the list is empty (i.e., the length is 0), return None.

Store a reference to the current tail node in a temporary variable.

If the list has only one node (i.e., the length is 1), set both the head and tail of the list to None.

If the list has more than one node, perform the following steps:

Update the tail of the list to be the previous node of the current tail.

Set the next attribute of the new tail node to None.

Set the prev attribute of the removed node (stored in the temporary variable) to None.

Decrement the length attribute of the list by 1.

Return the removed node (stored in the temporary variable).

Solution:

def pop(self):
        if self.length == 0:
            return None
        temp = self.tail
        if self.length == 1:
            self.head = None
            self.tail = None
        else:
            self.tail = self.tail.prev
            self.tail.next = None
            temp.prev = None
        self.length -= 1
        return temp
